Upstream zero-length MPEG frame validation adapted to 1.13.1.
Upstream: https://github.com/taglib/taglib/commit/b7dc1ab8acbfe341a76ab2e3b8e0a8c298abbe39

From b7dc1ab8acbfe341a76ab2e3b8e0a8c298abbe39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Urs Fleisch <ufleisch@users.sourceforge.net>
Date: Thu, 16 Nov 2023 18:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fail MPEG header check when frame length is zero (#1174)


--- a/taglib/mpeg/mpegheader.cpp
+++ b/taglib/mpeg/mpegheader.cpp
@@ -301,6 +301,11 @@
     // consistent. Otherwise, we assume that either or both of the frames are
     // broken.
 
+    // A frame length of 0 is probably invalid and would pass the test below
+    // because nextData would be the same as data.
+    if(d->frameLength == 0)
+      return;
+
     file->seek(offset + d->frameLength);
     const ByteVector nextData = file->readBlock(4);
 
